@@ -78,3 +78,22 @@ Under the hood, this will create or remove `tmp/email-dev.txt`.
 
 This gem depends on some private git repositories and it is not meant to be used by third parties. But we hope it can serve as inspiration for anyone wanting to run fizzy on their own infrastructure.
 
+
+### Languages
+
+Fizzy defaults to English. Visit any page with `?locale=ja` to switch to
+Japanese, or `?locale=en` to switch back. Before sign-in the choice lives in
+that browser session. Once authenticated it belongs to the identity, across
+its accounts. An unsupported locale has no effect.
+
+App-owned strings are in `config/locales/en.yml` and `config/locales/ja.yml`.
+Use `t` in views, `I18n.t` in Ruby, and `I18n.l` for human-readable server
+dates (not for URLs, JSON timestamps or DOM IDs). Translate whole messages
+with named interpolations, including hidden labels and native bridge titles.
+Only the `javascript` section is sent to browser controllers. Mail is rendered
+in the recipient's locale; user-authored content is never translated.
+
+The mounted Mission Control dashboard supplies English-only templates. Its
+Japanese variants live under `app/views/{layouts/,}mission_control/jobs`;
+check them when upgrading `mission_control-jobs`. The rich-text editor's own
+JavaScript messages are left as shipped by the editor.
